  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.4.0\n\n### Fixes\n- A markdown heading or code block (or any block kind registered for a `Paragraph` subclass) is written as a paragraph. The writer recognised only the built-in paragraph kind and dropped these blocks with their text.\n\n### Features\n- Bookmarks round-trip, so table of contents entries and cross-references (`w:hyperlink w:anchor`) navigate after loading. A `w:bookmarkStart` names the paragraph holding it (`Block.Bookmarks`); one between paragraphs names the next paragraph, and Word's `_GoBack` last-edit marker is skipped. Writing puts a `w:bookmarkStart`/`w:bookmarkEnd` pair around the content of every named paragraph, in the body, a list or a table cell, with ids unique in the document. The model keeps a bookmark's start only, so a bookmark that covered part of a paragraph or several paragraphs comes back around its whole first paragraph.\n- A markdown heading that a link targets by its slug (`[x](#getting-started)`) is written as a bookmark under that slug, so the link navigates in Word. A heading no link targets gets none.",
